# Filing status

> Module SaraStatus

> Using SaraWorld as W
> Using SaraPredicates as P
> Using SaraKinship as K
> Using Section7703 as S7703
> Using Section2 as S2

Filing status is what selects a rate schedule in §1, an applicable amount in
§68, and a standard deduction in §63. Determining it means consulting §7703
(married or not), §2(a) (surviving spouse) and §2(b) (head of household), all of
which sit on the statutes' dependency cycles.

Each is read the way the cases supply it — 26 inject `s7703/4`, 19 inject
`s2_a/3`, 19 inject `s2_b/3` — **falling back to derivation where the case does
not inject**, which is Pattern 1 of `SaraPattern.catala_en`: the injection is an
exception over a derived base case.

Marital status derives from §7703 (level 1 of the stratification in
`Section7703.catala_en`, so no cycle). §2(a) and §2(b) derive from `Section2`,
which is possible because §2 no longer reaches §151(d) — see the note on
`HouseholdForParent` there, and the cycle discussion in `sara_port/README.md`.

The kinship relations are rebuilt here from `world` rather than taken as
inputs, so that adding the §2 fallback did not change this scope's signature
and every caller downstream of it.

## Joint returns

`joint_return_(J), agent_(J,Taxp), agent_(J,Spouse), start_(J,first_day),
end_(J,last_day)` — the return must span the whole taxable year, which the
Prolog enforces by unifying the start and end against the year boundaries
rather than by comparing them.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope JointReturn:
  input world content W.World
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  ## `agent_(J,Spouse)`: the return has to name the *spouse* too, and `Spouse`
  ## is bound by the `s7703(Taxp,Spouse,_,Taxy)` that precedes it. Dropping
  ## this conjunct let a return signed by the taxpayer alone count as joint.
  input expected_spouse content optional of W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## Is there a joint return by this taxpayer covering the whole year?
  output filed content boolean
  ## The co-agent on that return, when there is one.
  output spouse content optional of W.Entity
```

```catala
scope JointReturn:
  definition filed equals
    exists ev among world.events such that
      ev.kinds contains W.EventKind.JointReturn
      and ev.agents contains taxpayer
      # No spouse, no `s7703(Taxp,Spouse,_,Taxy)`, so the clause never reaches
      # the joint return at all.
      and (match expected_spouse with pattern
           -- Absent: false
           -- Present content sp: ev.agents contains sp)
      and ev.starts contains (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)
      and ev.ends contains (W.last_day_year of taxable_year)

  definition spouse equals
    List.first_element of
      (combine all others
        among (map each ev among
                (list of e among world.events
                 such that e.kinds contains W.EventKind.JointReturn
                           and e.agents contains taxpayer
                           and e.starts contains (W.first_day_year of taxable_year)
                           and e.ends contains (W.last_day_year of taxable_year))
              to (list of a among ev.agents such that a.id != taxpayer.id))
        in acc initially []
        with acc ++ others)
```

## Status

`s1_c/4` is the residual case and states the test explicitly: not a surviving
spouse, not a head of household, and not married. The four statuses are mutually
exclusive in that reading, and (A) covers both the joint-return and the
surviving-spouse routes.

```catala-metadata
declaration enumeration Status:
  -- JointOrSurvivingSpouse
  -- HeadOfHousehold
  -- Unmarried
  -- MarriedFilingSeparately

declaration scope FilingStatus:
  input world content W.World
  input injections content list of W.Injection
  input taxpayer content W.Entity
  input taxable_year content integer
  ## §7703: is the taxpayer married for the taxable year?
  output married content boolean
  ## §2(a): surviving spouse
  output surviving_spouse content boolean
  ## §2(b): head of household
  output head_of_household content boolean
  output joint_return content boolean
  ## The spouse, where §7703 identifies one.
  output spouse content optional of W.Entity
  ## Rebuilt from `world` so this scope's signature stays stable.
  output child_of content list of K.Kinship
  output sibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  output descendent_of content list of K.Kinship
  output stepsibling_of content list of K.Kinship
  output stepparent_of content list of K.Kinship
  output child_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output parent_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output sibling_in_law_of content list of K.Kinship
  output status content Status
```

```catala
scope FilingStatus:
  definition child_of equals
    (output of K.Kinships with { -- world: world }).child_of
  definition sibling_of equals
    (output of K.Kinships with { -- world: world }).sibling_of
  definition descendent_of equals
    (output of K.Kinships with { -- world: world }).descendent_of
  definition stepsibling_of equals
    (output of K.InLaws with { -- world: world -- child_of: child_of
       -- sibling_of: sibling_of }).stepsibling_of
  definition stepparent_of equals
    (output of K.InLaws with { -- world: world -- child_of: child_of
       -- sibling_of: sibling_of }).stepparent_of
  definition child_in_law_of equals
    (output of K.InLaws with { -- world: world -- child_of: child_of
       -- sibling_of: sibling_of }).child_in_law_of
  definition parent_in_law_of equals
    (output of K.InLaws with { -- world: world -- child_of: child_of
       -- sibling_of: sibling_of }).parent_in_law_of
  definition sibling_in_law_of equals
    (output of K.InLaws with { -- world: world -- child_of: child_of
       -- sibling_of: sibling_of }).sibling_in_law_of

  ## §7703 derived, with the case's injection as an overriding exception.
  definition married equals
    (output of S7703.MaritalStatusA with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).married
  exception definition married
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s7703_4,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true

  ## §2(a), derived, with the case's grant as an overriding exception.
  definition surviving_spouse equals
    (output of S2.SurvivingSpouse with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds
    # A grant that *replaced* `s2_a/3` leaves the statute no clauses of its
    # own, so only the rows answer and the exception below is the whole story.
    and not (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s2_a_3)

  exception definition surviving_spouse
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s2_a_3,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true

  ## §2(b), likewise. The dependant is left unbound, as every caller does.
  definition head_of_household equals
    (output of S2.HeadOfHousehold with {
       -- injections: injections -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- dependant: Absent -- taxable_year: taxable_year
       -- child_of: child_of -- sibling_of: sibling_of
       -- descendent_of: descendent_of -- stepsibling_of: stepsibling_of
       -- stepparent_of: stepparent_of
       -- child_in_law_of: child_in_law_of
       -- parent_in_law_of: parent_in_law_of
       -- sibling_in_law_of: sibling_in_law_of }).holds
    and not (W.pred_overridden of injections, P.pred_s2_b_3)

  exception definition head_of_household
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s2_b_3,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals true

  ## The spouse, likewise derived with the case's grant overriding. `married`
  ## already honours an injected `s7703/4`; the *identity* has to come from the
  ## same place, because a case can grant the marriage without the event base
  ## naming one — and §63(c)(2)(A)(i) then asks whether that named spouse
  ## signed the joint return.
  definition spouse equals
    (output of S7703.MaritalStatusA with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).spouse
  exception definition spouse
    under condition
      (W.injected_holds of injections, P.pred_s7703_4,
         [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])
    consequence equals
      (match (List.first_element of
                (W.injections_for of injections, P.pred_s7703_4,
                   [taxpayer.id; -1; -1; W.num_key of taxable_year])) with pattern
       -- Absent: Absent
       -- Present content inj: W.injection_entity of inj, 2)

  definition joint_return equals
    (output of JointReturn with {
       -- world: world -- taxpayer: taxpayer -- expected_spouse: spouse
       -- taxable_year: taxable_year }).filed

  ## §1's four clauses are a *disjunction* and SARA backtracks over every one
  ## that holds, so a taxpayer who is both a head of household and a surviving
  ## spouse has two taxes and `tax/3` accepts either. A single `status` has to
  ## choose --- and choosing nothing is not an option: as unlabelled siblings
  ## these three conflicted and the interpreter refused the program outright
  ## rather than answering it. The priority is §1's own clause order, (a)
  ## before (b) before (c) and (d), which is the solution SARA reaches first.
  ## `Unmarried` stays the base: §1(c) demands `\+ s7703(Taxp,_,_,Taxy)` and so
  ## cannot hold beside (d)'s married-filing-separately anyway. See D81.
  definition status equals Status.Unmarried

  label filing_separately
  exception definition status
    under condition married and not joint_return
    consequence equals Status.MarriedFilingSeparately

  label head_of_household_status
  exception filing_separately definition status
    under condition head_of_household
    consequence equals Status.HeadOfHousehold

  exception head_of_household_status definition status
    under condition (married and joint_return) or surviving_spouse
    consequence equals Status.JointOrSurvivingSpouse
```
